Retired shop teacher here, and a bit nervous about showing this to anyone. I wanted Roman numerals for my woodworking labels:
def to_roman(n):
    if not 0 < n < 4000:
        raise ValueError('Use 1-3999')
    out = []
    for v, s in ((1000,'M'),(900,'CM'),(500,'D'),(400,'CD'),(100,'C'),(90,'XC'),(50,'L'),(40,'XL'),(10,'X'),(9,'IX'),(5,'V'),(4,'IV'),(1,'I')):
        count, n = divmod(n, v)
        out.append(s * count)
    return ''.join(out)
Any feedback?

