function draw(tickets, n) {
  const pool = [...tickets];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const j = i + Math.floor(Math.random() * (pool.length - i));
    [pool[i], pool[j]] = [pool[j], pool[i]];
  }
  return pool.slice(0, n);
}
```

Dad of three, coding in the evenings after bedtime. This is a caching wrapper I wrote for my daughter's homework tracker. Curious what you'd say.
