I'm a structural engineer in Stuttgart, and I write JavaScript as a hobby. Here's my prime generator. I'd value your opinion on it.
```js
function* primes() {
  const seen = new Map();
  for (let n = 2; ; n++) {
    const ps = seen.get(n);
    if (!ps) { yield n; seen.set(n * n, [n]); continue; }
    seen.delete(n);
    for (const p of ps) seen.set(n + p, [...(seen.get(n + p) ?? []), p]);
  }
}
```

